{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And upon their gods YHWH executed judgments.</b> He fulfilled what He said (Exodus 12:12): ״ובכל אלהי מצרים אעשה שפטים אני ה׳״ — \"and against all the gods of Egypt I will execute judgments, I am YHWH.\" And the judgments were: if they were of silver or gold they melted, if of wood they rotted, if of stone they shattered. And further, 'judgments' includes the manner of what is written (I Samuel 5:4): ״והנה דגון נופל לפניו ארצה לפני ארון ה׳ וראש דגון ושתי כפות ידיו כרותות אל המפתן״ — \"and behold Dagon was fallen face-ward to the ground before the ark of YHWH; and the head of Dagon and his two hands were cut off upon the threshold.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:37:41.451803120Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}